content.text:
Need verify `loadWorkspaceFiles` function exists? Search. It might not, condition checks typeof. Fine.

Now CSS:
- `.modal-backdrop.active` exists. Add `.modal-backdrop.open` too for safety? Not needed but could. We changed JS to active.
- Add XP window button styling.
- Add boot logo styles.

Let's edit CSS for XP buttons. Where to put? Near XP section. We'll add after universal contrast section maybe after `.btn-primary` exception. Need selectors to beat `.btn-secondary` and color enforcement.

Important: current `.xp-window *:not(...) { color:#000 !important; }` forces black text on all, including `.btn-primary` but exception later `.btn-primary` white. Our new rules must come after line 6098 and be specific enough. Add:

```
.xp-window .btn,
.xp-dialog-body .btn,
.xp-cpl-body .btn {
  background: linear-gradient(180deg,#fff 0%,#f4f3ee 48%,#e6e4da 100%) !important;
  border: 1px solid #8e8c84 !important;
  border-radius: 3px !important;
  color:#000 !important;
  box-shadow: inset 0 1px 0 #fff !important;
  text-shadow:none !important;
  font-family: Tahoma, Arial, sans-serif !important;
}
...
.xp-window .btn-primary, .xp-dialog-body .btn-primary ... {
 background: linear-gradient(180deg,#3a9bff,#0053ee) !important;
 border-color:#003c74 !important;
 color:#fff !important;
}
```
Also `.xp-window .btn:disabled` grey.

But maybe `.xp-dialog-body *:not(.btn-primary)` applies color black to child spans; our button has text nodes only.

Also `.btn` global border none. Fine.

What about WLM toolbar buttons: not inside `.xp-window`, no change. The left dark theme buttons remain dark; intended.

Let's insert after line around `.btn-primary, .btn-primary *` in the contrast fixes.

